00:38:16.080 --> 00:38:19.230
at the University of
California, Los Angeles.

00:38:19.230 --> 00:38:21.150
I wanted to take the opportunity

00:38:21.150 --> 00:38:22.500
to examine these collections

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:24.900
in conjunction to research the period

00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:27.900
between the Federal Highway Act of 1956

00:38:27.900 --> 00:38:32.900
and the Rebuild LA Program
created by then Mayor Tom Bradley

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:38.320
to rebuild Los Angeles after
the Los Angeles uprisings

00:38:39.600 --> 00:38:43.140
in order to study urban
disinvestment and reinvestment,

00:38:43.140 --> 00:38:48.140
specifically how Latinx and
small businesses reacted

00:38:48.270 --> 00:38:50.610
to changes in government spending.

00:38:50.610 --> 00:38:52.830
Although I had intended
to spend equal amounts

00:38:52.830 --> 00:38:54.330
of time on both collections,

00:38:54.330 --> 00:38:56.610
I ended up focusing a majority of my time

00:38:56.610 --> 00:38:57.900
on the Bradley collection

00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:02.130
because it centered businesses
as a backbone of Los Angeles.

00:39:02.130 --> 00:39:05.370
With this, three different themes emerged.

00:39:05.370 --> 00:39:09.240
One was the language that the
City of Los Angeles employed

00:39:09.240 --> 00:39:11.190
after the Los Angeles uprisings

00:39:11.190 --> 00:39:14.430
in order to establish diversity
as a positive strength

00:39:14.430 --> 00:39:17.190
and itself as a microcosm of the nation

00:39:17.190 --> 00:39:20.670
in order to continue to attract business.

00:39:20.670 --> 00:39:23.340
Two was how they treated
the homeless population

00:39:23.340 --> 00:39:24.240
during their efforts

00:39:24.240 --> 00:39:28.770
to recentralize LA's
downtown business district.

00:39:28.770 --> 00:39:31.800
And finally how Latinx
businesses were writing

00:39:31.800 --> 00:39:34.560
to express different social
and political concerns

00:39:34.560 --> 00:39:35.583
during this time.

00:39:37.110 --> 00:39:38.802
For instance, I included a letter

00:39:38.802 --> 00:39:42.870
from the Mexican Grocers Association

00:39:42.870 --> 00:39:45.210
that wrote to express discontent

00:39:45.210 --> 00:39:48.780
after a government agent from
the INS came to give a talk

00:39:48.780 --> 00:39:51.840
and implied that immigrants
were drug dealers.

00:39:51.840 --> 00:39:53.550
This is exemplary of different,

00:39:53.550 --> 00:39:56.190
of how different businesses
were not only writing

00:39:56.190 --> 00:39:57.450
about fiscal concerns,

00:39:57.450 --> 00:40:00.363
but also about social
and political concerns.

00:40:01.770 --> 00:40:03.630
Overall, my summer research,

00:40:03.630 --> 00:40:05.370
specifically on the Bradley collection,

00:40:05.370 --> 00:40:07.920
helped me identify different stakeholders

00:40:07.920 --> 00:40:10.110
amongst Latinx businesses

00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:13.440
and how the city was
attempting to rebrand itself

00:40:13.440 --> 00:40:15.270
to continue attracting business,

00:40:15.270 --> 00:40:18.240
and finally, how it was
prioritizing different businesses

00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:19.140
and different people

00:40:19.140 --> 00:40:22.560
in order to attempt to recentralize.

00:40:22.560 --> 00:40:25.740
And the Roybal collection
allowed me to get some context

00:40:25.740 --> 00:40:28.530
on the Federal Highway Act.

00:40:28.530 --> 00:40:29.883
Thank you very much.

